<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pyxis of al-Mughira</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">968</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pyxis of al-Mughira is a carved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> box made in 968 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madinat-al-zahra">Madinat al-Zahra</a> for al-Mughira, a younger son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a>. Its densely carved medallions show courtly scenes, musicians, hunters and animals, and an Arabic inscription records its date and owner. It is among the finest works of Córdoban ivory carving and is now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louvre">Louvre</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pyxis-of-al-mughira.jpg" alt="Pyxis of al-Mughira" width="320" height="485" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop at the court of Medina Azahara · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pyxid_Al_Mughira_OA_4068.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
